---
import About from "./index.astro";
import Trivia from "../../components/about/Trivia";

import { getLastUpdated } from "../../scripts/page-last-updated";
const pageLastUpdated = getLastUpdated(import.meta.url);
---

<About title="Trivia & Fun Facts" pageLastUpdated={pageLastUpdated}>
    <div id="trivia" class="section-header text-font">
        <p>Trivia</p>
        <hr />
        <p class="section-desc">
            How much have you learned? Let's check and see with this trivia
            quiz! Good luck, or should I say "soohm /hl/ihmaud eihne ihd
            dohth"...
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-20">
        <Trivia client:load />
    </div>

    <div id="fun-facts" class="section-header text-font">
        <p>Fun Facts</p>
        <hr />
    </div>
    <section class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-font">
        <div>
            <p class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">
                1. The Origins of Island Shapes and Names
            </p>
            <img
                src="/sohcoffeeuh.png"
                alt="Photograph of a plate of balsamic vinegar and oil that resembles the shape of the continent Sohq'authuh."
                class="size-35 sm:size-50 object-cover float-right ml-4 mb-1"
            />
            <p>
                Back in July of 2023, I first started working on the design of
                the planet Mk&deg;mih' oh, and on one particular day, I decided
                to try local coffee shop I hadn't been to yet. La Fontana Caffe
                had an item on the menu &ndash; $5.00 Foccacia Bread with olive
                oil and balsamic &ndash; that I decided to try. The food was
                delicious, and when I saw the remnants of my meal, I decided two
                things:
            </p>
            <ul class="my-2 pl-4">
                <li>1. This would be a super cool shape for a continent</li>
                <li>
                    2. I must remember this meal forever by naming said
                    continent after it
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-2">
                And so, the spill of vinegar and oil became Sohq'authuh, names
                after the "Foccacia" bread, and Dau/hl/saumik&deg; (which I
                designed based on the foam in my empty mug of coffee) was named
                after the "Balsamic" vinegar.
            </p>
            <p>Unfortunately, La Fontana Caffee is now closed.</p>
            <div class="clear-both"></div>
        </div>

        <div>
            <p class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">2. Terrible Naming Skills</p>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                <p>
                    This section will also answer the question "Why are Einasvel
                    and Enausq'/hl/ used interchangeably?"
                </p>
                <p>
                    Funny story, because I'm completely terrible at naming
                    things, I was stuck on what to call this species at first. I
                    eventually spotted a thing of Vaseline on my desk and
                    resorted to rearranging the letters until I came up with
                    Einasvel. After later creating the language and sounds, I
                    translated it into the closest thing, Enausq'/hl/, which is
                    why you see those words used interchangeably throughout this
                    site!
                </p>
                <p>
                    A similar reasoning is used for Mikimoh and Mk&deg;mih' oh,
                    although in this case, the proper spelling "Mk&deg;mih' oh"
                    was actually created first, and Mikimoh was only created
                    after as a way for the planets name to be pronounced easily
                    using sounds more familiar to humans.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</About>
